<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Third Battle of Panipat</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1761</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Third Battle of Panipat was fought in 1761 near Panipat in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha Empire</a> and the invading army of the Afghan ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-shah-abdali">Ahmad Shah Durrani</a> and his allies. It was one of the largest battles of the eighteenth century and ended in a crushing Maratha defeat with very heavy losses. The Maratha Empire profile treats it as a turning point that halted Maratha expansion in the north.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/third-battle-of-panipat.jpg" alt="Third Battle of Panipat" width="320" height="250" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Third_battle_of_Panipat_13_January_1761.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
